# Release Log — alice branch (changes from 0.1-alpha)

## bullet_drone

2 commits, 9 files changed, +724 / -18 lines.

### New files

- `src/bullet_drone/isaac_physics.py` (388 lines)
  Isaac PhysX physics backend. Mirrors PyBulletPhysics interface (reset, step,
  hold, close, raycasting). Lazy-inits a shared headless SimulationApp, builds
  a USD stage with physics scene, ground plane, and rigid-body drone. Applies
  body-frame forces rotated to world frame via quaternion. Reads state from USD
  prim attributes. target_contact/terrain_contact stubbed to False.

- `src/launcher/isaac_renderer.py` (136 lines)
  Isaac Sim renderer process manager. Launches python.sh with the
  bullet_render isaac/main.py script. Manages ZMQ image transport and
  shared-memory frame reading. Waits for first rendered frame before
  declaring ready.

- `src/launcher/__main__.py` (3 lines)
  Enables `python -m launcher` entry point.

- `tools/isaacSimKillAll.bash`
  Kill script for all Isaac stack processes (Isaac Sim, SITL, bullet_visual,
  launcher).

### Modified files

- `src/launcher/cli.py`
  Added CLI options: --renderer-backend (godot|isaac), --physics-backend
  (pybullet|isaac), --isaac-headless, --world.

- `src/launcher/main.py`
  Conditional import of IsaacRenderer/IsaacPhysics based on backend choice.

- `tools/run_target_scene.sh`
  Added --isaac, --isaac-physics, --isaac-headless, --world flags.
  Auto-detects SITL binary. Launches via python.sh when using Isaac physics.

- `tools/run_app_after_sitl.sh`
  File mode change (644 → 755).

- `libs/bullet_image_transport/src/bullet_image_transport/shm.py`
  Added optional host_capture_ns parameter to FrameWriter.write() for
  host-side capture timestamp passthrough from Isaac renderer.
